Tremor (libvorbisidec), the Xiph.Org Foundation's integer Vorbis decoder,
vendored for the RPi's Ogg Vorbis decoding (gpu/audio/vorbis.c), with the
parts of libogg it needs:

- *.c, *.h, COPYING: https://gitlab.xiph.org/xiph/tremor, commit 820fb32
  (2025-04-03), unchanged; without vorbisfile.c (files: the host reads them)
  and the build files.
- libogg/: bitwise.c, framing.c, crctable.h, COPYING from
  https://gitlab.xiph.org/xiph/ogg, commit 06a5e02 (2026-03-02), unchanged.
- ogg/: that libogg's ogg.h and os_types.h, unchanged, and config_types.h,
  which libogg's configure writes, written here (the types Tremor's own
  config_types.h has).
- compat/: written here, the C library functions they need that Circle
  hasn't (toupper, labs, memchr).

